Jane and Jack talk about grammar syntax. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Listen to the audio. Move the sentences up or down\n<span class=\"sena-icon sena-icon-vertical-drag\"></span> to put\nthem in the correct order.\n", "type": "text"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob08re6aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 9, "type": "MT1"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "type": "RSLT"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "enpe7n2le01ob08re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "  ", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n2le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "<strong>Sergio</strong>: Hi, Cristian. I would like us to practice the topic of language syntax, you know, we cannot fail that exam. </br>\n<strong>Christian</strong>: Sure! Let's review the topic. So far I remember, the syntax of a language defines whether or not the language is legal and if we can execute it successfully. </br>\n<strong>Sergio</strong>: Yeah, I also remember that the language syntax has nothing to do with the functions of the program but with the grammar. </br>", "image": "enpe7n2le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "29000", "text": "<strong>Christian</strong>: Do you understand the concept of grammar? </br>\n<strong>Sergio</strong>: Yes, a grammar is a set of rules that define how to make statements, which are like sentences; those statements are made of tokens that are groups of characters equivalent to words in human languages. </br>\n<strong>Christian</strong>: You're right. Then we can use the Extended Backus Form to define grammar; this notation differentiates terminal symbols or single tokens from nonterminal symbols, that means a sequence of tokens. We define nonterminal symbols using grammar rules that show us the expanded sequence of detailed tokens. To read the grammar we start from left to right always with a nonterminal symbol. </br>\n<strong>Sergio</strong>: We can use the EBNF to verify if a statement is legal, right? </br>", "image": "enpe7n2le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "81000", "text": "<strong>Christian</strong>: You can also use it to generate statements. </br>\n<strong>Sergio</strong>: Ok, anything else we are missing? </br>\n<strong>Christian</strong>: Yeah, the EBNF defines context-free grammars that always generate the same token fragments in the non-terminal variables. There are other techniques to read context-sensitive grammars that depend on the context to run. </br>\n<strong>Sergio</strong>:  I want to add that in order to avoid ambiguity in our sentences, we have to add as many conditions as necessary because changing the syntax of the program can be a very complex process.  </br>\n<strong>Christian</strong>: I think we are ready for the exam.</br>", "image": "enpe7n2le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n2le01ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}